ANGLE: accept blank lines before #version 300 es and later

ANGLE's preprocessor rejected #version 300 es and later unless it sat on
the very first line. Qualcomm's frame generation library starts every
shader with a newline, which Qualcomm's and Mesa's compilers accept, so
none of its shaders compiled. Blank lines and comments may now come
first; any other token before #version is still an error.

diff --git a/src/compiler/preprocessor/DirectiveParser.cpp b/src/compiler/preprocessor/DirectiveParser.cpp
index ab6f9a2..bcd6a30 100644
--- a/src/compiler/preprocessor/DirectiveParser.cpp
+++ b/src/compiler/preprocessor/DirectiveParser.cpp
@@ -790,12 +790,8 @@ void DirectiveParser::parseVersion(Token *token)
         valid = false;
     }
 
-    if (valid && version >= 300 && token->location.line > 1)
-    {
-        mDiagnostics->report(Diagnostics::PP_VERSION_NOT_FIRST_LINE_ESSL3, token->location,
-                             token->text);
-        valid = false;
-    }
+    // Droidloom: blank lines and comments may precede #version 300 es and later, as Qualcomm's
+    // and Mesa's compilers allow.  Anything else before it is still PP_VERSION_NOT_FIRST_STATEMENT.
 
     if (valid)
     {
